Use these sound files with scidCommunity.

Select this directory: Options -> Resources -> Sound files folder
(Or Scid will switch to it automatically when Spanish is the active language.)

Spoken Spanish move announcements, generated with the open-source Piper
text-to-speech engine using the "es_ES-davefx-medium" voice.

  Piper engine : https://github.com/rhasspy/piper  (MIT license)
  Voice model  : https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices  (MIT license,
                 voice es_ES-davefx-medium)

Spoken tokens (piece names, files, ranks and special announcements):

    King=rey, Queen=dama, Rook=torre, Bishop=alfil, Knight=caballo
    CastleK=enroque corto, CastleQ=enroque largo
    Back=atrás, Mate=jaque mate, Promote=promoción, Check=jaque,
    alert=alerta, x=por
    files: a, be, ce, de, e, efe, ge, hache
    ranks: uno, dos, tres, cuatro, cinco, seis, siete, ocho

The move/event sounds (move.wav, move_capture.wav, move_castling.wav,
move_check.wav, move_promotion.wav, move_normal.wav) are copied unchanged
from the base sounds/ directory, so "Move sound only" mode still uses the
default (non-spoken) sounds.
